{
  "cliqueSealDifficulty": {
    "_info": {
      "comment": "EIP-225's in-turn / out-of-turn difficulty rule, as accept/reject PAIRS. A signer whose turn it is at this height must seal at difficulty 2; any other authorized signer must seal at 1. Each vector is two headers differing in the difficulty field and nothing else that is not downstream of it -- one a correct client accepts, one it refuses.",
      "whyEACHCaseIsAPAIR": "The accepted half is the CONTROL and is the load-bearing one. A client that refuses every block scores perfectly against rejection vectors alone, so a rejection with no matching acceptance measures nothing. The two halves differ in `difficulty`, and consequently in `extraData` (the seal is over a different header), `sealHash`, `hash` and `rlp` -- that cascade is expected and is not a second variable.",
      "bothDirectionsAppearBecauseTheRuleHasTWOBRANCHES": "go-ethereum returns errWrongDifficulty from two separate conditions -- in-turn-but-not-2, and out-of-turn-but-not-1 -- so a client can implement one and omit the other. One vector fires each. A single-direction file would score a half-implemented client as correct.",
      "howAHarnessReadsThis": "Build the genesis from `genesisSigners` exactly as in clique_signer_voting.json and confirm `genesis.hash`. Then import `acceptedHeader`: it MUST be accepted. Separately, from the same genesis, import `rejectedHeader`: it MUST be refused. Do not import both onto one chain -- they are siblings at the same height, not a sequence.",
      "whyThisFileExists": "No shared vector for this rule exists anywhere. Measured 2026-08-25: errWrongDifficulty appears in ethereum/go-ethereum and core-geth ONLY in clique.go -- its definition and two return sites -- and in no test file in either repository, control errRecentlySigned appearing in snapshot_test.go in both, so the instrument reads tests. The upstream scenario table cannot reach it: it sets fakeDiff, which disables exactly this check.",
      "besuDOESTestItAndThatNarrowsTheClaim": "besu carries CliqueDifficultyValidationRule and CliqueDifficultyValidationRuleTest, which asserts all four combinations. So the correct claim is NOT that the rule is untested -- it is that no CROSS-CLIENT vector exists, and that besu's own coverage runs against a mocked ValidatorProvider rather than a real signed chain. Stated here because the wider claim is the one a reader will assume.",
      "oracle": "ethereum/go-ethereum consensus/clique, RUN not read. Each rejected header was inserted and the recorded error is what InsertChain returned; each accepted header was inserted into an independent chain and confirmed to succeed.",
      "oracle-version": "ethereum/go-ethereum master @ af7c0fd8e, pulled 2026-08-25",
      "crossImplementation": "EXECUTED by a second implementation, 2026-08-25. besu (Java, root commit 7dfc2e408 -- a lineage sharing nothing with go-ethereum) at 182e5ba749 was run against these exact vectors through its own CliqueDifficultyValidationRule. It accepted both acceptedHeaders, refused both rejectedHeaders, and refused them in BOTH directions with its own diagnostics -- \"difficulty 1 does not equal expected difficulty 2\" and \"difficulty 2 does not equal expected difficulty 1\". It also recomputed all six recorded header hashes (genesis, accepted and rejected for each vector) identically, and recovered the same proposer address from each seal that go-ethereum recorded. Two implementations, two languages, no shared code.",
      "generated": "2026-08-25",
      "wrongBuildMethod": "Each branch of the rule was deleted from ethereum/go-ethereum's verifySeal in turn, leaving a half-implemented client. Both patches were confirmed to change the source and to compile. The unmodified build is the control and catches nothing (2/2 pass).",
      "wrongBuildScores": {
        "difficulty_inturn_branch_only": "1/2 -- fails out_of_turn_header_given_in_turn_difficulty, and only that one.",
        "difficulty_outofturn_branch_only": "1/2 -- fails in_turn_header_given_out_of_turn_difficulty, and only that one.",
        "theTwoSetsAreDISJOINT": "Measured, not reasoned. Each half-implemented build fails precisely the vector aimed at the branch it dropped, so neither vector is dead weight and a one-direction file would pass a client missing half the rule.",
        "siblingFileScores": "Both defects score 0/24 against clique_signer_voting.json. The voting file cannot see this rule, which is the measured reason these are two files and not one."
      },
      "aHARNESSMUSTREADchainConfigFIRST": "These headers are London-era and carry 16 RLP fields. A client configured outside that window fails at decode, before any rule is reached. `chainConfig` states exactly what to set; do not infer it from the genesis fields.",
      "whatTheBesuRunDOESNotClose": "besu's validator set was supplied from this file's own genesisSigners rather than derived. For THIS rule that is the declared input, not a mock of the subject: the difficulty rule consumes a validator set and a parent and decides a difficulty. Deriving the set from headers is a different rule -- the sibling voting file's -- and supplying it there WOULD be circular. So what remains open is a full chain import in which besu derives the set through its own BlockValidatorProvider and VoteTallyCache; that is the voting file's cross-check, not this one's.",
      "besuOwnCoverageStillNarrowerThanThis": "besu's CliqueDifficultyValidationRuleTest asserts all four combinations but builds its headers with a test fixture. These headers were sealed by a different client entirely and besu recovered the signer from the signature -- which is the part no single client's own suite can exercise.",
      "corroboratedByMUTATIONNotOnlyByGrep": "The claim that the geth lineage does not test this rule was established here by searching for errWrongDifficulty against a control. core-geth's own oracle-wiring pass reached the same conclusion independently and by a different method, 2026-08-25: mutating diffInTurn from 2 to 3 changed the source, compiled, and its entire consensus/clique suite still PASSED. The cause is structural rather than an oversight -- every diffInTurn reference in those tests is the constant itself (clique_test.go lines 66 and 84, snapshot_test.go line 449), so subject and assertion move together and no mutation of it can ever fail. A grep and a mutation test agreeing is stronger evidence than either alone."
    },
    "chainConfig": {
      "comment": "What a client must configure for its header decoder and validator to accept these chains. Recorded because it is NOT derivable from the vectors, and a wrong guess fails at RLP decode -- which reads as a broken fixture rather than a misconfigured harness.",
      "headerFieldCount": 16,
      "whyTheFieldCountMatters": "16 fields is the London-era header: 15 pre-London, 16 with baseFeePerGas, 17 once Shanghai adds withdrawalsRoot, 20 at Cancun. A client configured outside that window cannot decode these headers at all, and the failure looks nothing like a consensus disagreement.",
      "activatedAtBlockZero": [
        "Homestead",
        "EIP150",
        "EIP155",
        "EIP158",
        "Byzantium",
        "Constantinople",
        "Petersburg",
        "Istanbul",
        "MuirGlacier",
        "Berlin",
        "London",
        "ArrowGlacier",
        "GrayGlacier"
      ],
      "notActivated": "No time-based fork. Shanghai, Cancun, Prague and everything later are unset -- which is what keeps the header at 16 fields.",
      "daoForkSupport": false,
      "terminalTotalDifficulty": "0x7fffffffffffffff -- effectively unreachable, so these chains never merge and stay under the Clique engine throughout.",
      "chainIdUsedToGenerate": 1,
      "chainIdIsNOTAnInputAndThatWasMEASURED": "The whole vector set was regenerated with chainId 61 and the output is BYTE-IDENTICAL to chainId 1. That is the evidence for filing this under proposals/ rather than under a network: no chain id reaches the rule, and the value above is a generator artifact a harness may set to anything.",
      "genesisAllocIsEMPTY": "stateRoot 0x56e81f171bcc55a6ff8345e692c0f86e5b48e01b996cadc001622fb5e363b421 is the empty trie root. There are no accounts, no transactions and no ommers in any vector."
    },
